mantle rm428
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_berit_wickton
title the spoon star
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=servant warmth=warm
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk takes_the_last_steps_in_pairs_to_catch_a_star_in_a_spoon
likes smoked_eel stars tidy_house first_snow
dislikes waiting salt_wind
fears a_quiet_kindness_taken_for_an_obligation
hopes a_clear_upper_window_at_the_end_of_work
topics pastimes +0.5 work +0.5 home +0.4 weather +0.2
styles comfort=welcome gossip=reticent refuse=gentle tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# takes the final stair in two eager strides to catch a first star in the curve of a clean spoon and treats a late meal with the same care as a grand dinner.

words
oath! = Six clouded spoons | A whole tray of moons
saying! = Keep a corner of the sky | The last bowl deserves a shine
spoon = a polished spoon | the little bright spoon
bowlcurve = the silver hollow | a shallow curve
rim = the fine rim | the curved edge
star = one steady pin of light | a pale low star
upperpane = the high pane | the upper corner
traycloth = a folded tray cloth | my soft cloth
eel = a twist of smoked fish | the dark eel strip
stairpair = the last two risers | a pair of steps
drape = a loose curtain | the fine hanging
sootdot = a little grey fleck | the dark speck
tuck = a turned hem | an inward corner
snowlight = the white glow | a pale wash

any
opinion houses mixed 0 : A fine hall is at its most gracious when a late supper gets the same clean spoon as the first fine course.
opinion church for 1 : A little quiet reflection is a gift within reach of any ordinary kitchen.
opinion festivals for 1 : I'll enjoy a feast through its many ordinary details, including the meal that reaches the last guest.
opinion merchants mixed 0 : One sound spoon well polished is quite enough. I would examine the actual edge before paying for finery.
opinion road for 1 : The quiet road out towards the hills is worth taking while there is still a patch of evening overhead.
opinion city for 1 : A single star rising over the city can lend a blank kitchen wall the prettiest light.

grown
line greet : Welcome. I can leave the polishing by me. | Hello. There's a clear place where the tray won't be in the way.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : Your first visit to my little patch of shine. Welcome. | A first greeting needn't be a grand one.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. A clean spoon shows the daylight already. | Early light at the high pane. Good morning.
line greet.return : Hello in return. I've folded the cloth quite away. | I heard you before the little reflection left the rim.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : A dear face just above the polished edge. | I can set a little bright place for you without ceremony.
line greet.return [here.time=night] : An excellent hour to look up as well as speak softly. | Hello. We've some evening sky left to enjoy.
line again.open : Back before the polish has quite lost its warmth. | Our ways have come together a second time very gently.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Come see a star I can hold within reach. | Here at the side of me. The light shows from this angle.
line farewell : May your last steps take you to a bright window. | May you have clear sky above your road.
line farewell.return : I'll put my spoon away and let you through. | A kindly evening or a kindly road, whichever comes first.
line react.news : I'll set the shining thing down and attend to your words. | Bring the account into the light at whatever pace suits you.
line react.news.new : I'd seen no faint reflection of that before now. | That's new enough to make me put the work aside.
line react.news.known : Yes. I remember that piece quite distinctly. | The earlier telling caught much the same light.
line react.news.doubt : I'd turn the words a little and see if the light goes with them. | Something in there looks more like an echo than an event.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|crime|assault|loss|theft] : I'll put a meal by and stay beside you through the telling. | Sad words have a right to be heard at their proper pace.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|work] : There is a quite lovely glimmer in that account. | I'd treasure good news of that sort through the rest of a shift.
line ask.how : Have you found a little clear spot in your day? | How has the work sat upon your shoulders?
line answer.how : A little tired, enjoying what small bright things I can see. | Fairly even, with a warm corner of feeling left for company.
line decline : I'd be failing an earlier promise if I offered my time as well. | I should like to help, but the little space I have is already claimed.
line accept_decline : I understand. One may keep one's quiet interval. | Then I'll put that request away with no ill will.
line preclose : There's a little stretch of light I should get to before the work resumes. | I'd best finish what was nearly bright when I set it aside.
line accept_preclose : You can go sweetly on to your next call. | Certainly. There's no virtue in keeping you waiting.
line thank : You kept me a little of the light. Thank you. | I appreciate a kindness done with that much care.
line deflect_thanks : It only needed one spare corner of cloth. | There was room on the tray for another small kindness.
line sympathise : You may sit here and let the bright chatter go past awhile. | My company is yours without requiring a cheerful expression.
line reassure : Small bright things survive a surprisingly grey evening. | Let's put the immediate load down and find a place to sit.
line ack : Yes, I see the light quite plainly there. | That has the shape you described.
line give.advice : Try changing your angle before polishing a perfectly clean thing. | Make a place for the last guest before serving the first.

scene catchstar
when topic=pastimes self.likes=stars
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can bring a star indoors on a spoon for a little while.
b : Does it need a very large spoon? | Which part holds the star?
a : Only a bright curve and a few degrees of patient tipping at the window. | At the inner rim. My wrist changes the view and the star keeps its own excellent place.

scene stairpair
when topic=work self.job=servant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When my tray is empty I take the last two steps together to catch the view above the rail.
b : Why the hurry? | Always the last two?
a : A light seen across a stair well may last a surprisingly short while. I enjoy finding it in time. | Only with the landing well in view and empty. No star's worth a startled guest.

scene lateplace
when topic=work self.job=servant self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like the late place set with a really bright spoon, not the one still waiting for the cloth.
b : Who would notice? | Would you polish one specially?
a : A wolf arriving tired and ready to feel an afterthought might notice. I should like to prevent that. | Yes. A few quiet turns of a cloth make an ordinary welcome feel properly meant.

scene trayturn
when topic=work self.job=servant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A shallow spoon weighs very little until it begins slipping under the rest of the tray.
b : Can you hear it move? | Can you keep it still?
a : One fine click, generally. A very small noise, worth attending to promptly. | I lay a strip of cloth where the handles come together. Less excitement and a kinder sound.

scene tidydrape
when topic=home self.likes=tidy_house
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A tidy window gives me rather more sky for no enlargement of the room. | I draw one curtain entirely clear of its little pane when my work ends.
b : Isn't that inviting a draught? | Do you value the room or the view?
a : The pane remains shut when it's cold. I was only inviting a little light to look in. | I like the sense of one being rather more generous on account of the other.

scene eelcurl
when topic=food self.likes=smoked_eel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I turn a strip of smoky eel into a loose curl on the plate.
b : Is the curl a piece of grandeur? | Does it taste different?
a : Only a convenient way to pick up a good firm strip. It happens to look rather handsome too. | No. But the edge comes readily to the fork and I'm free to enjoy the smoke instead of chasing supper.

scene snowshine
when topic=weather here.weather=snow
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Fresh snow lends a spoon a startlingly pale face compared with yesterday's grey light. | A new dusting seems to polish everything indoors by reflection.
b : You'd stop cleaning then? | Even an old spoon looks bright?
a : I still know the difference between clean and merely well lit. Quite nice to enjoy both at once. | Yes. A faint old scratch can almost lose itself in all that white.

scene saltpane
when topic=weather self.dislikes=salt_wind
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A sea wind salts the pane till the evening sky looks full of false stars. | A sharp salt breeze feels personally intent on putting every newly wiped thing back to work.
b : Do they still show when you move? | Is it the wind or the salt you mind?
a : No. Turn my head and those little marks stay on the glass. A real star shifts against the frame. | Both together. The wind alone is welcome to pass without leaving a gritty account of itself.

scene restnow
when topic=day self.dislikes=waiting
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd rather be told to take a real interval than stand waiting on the point of being summoned. | Waiting at a half-open door makes the minutes feel rather poorly arranged.
b : How would ten minutes be used? | Does a firm time help?
a : Climb right up to the highest pane and look out. A known short pause can be quite generous. | Immensely. I can put the tray on a surface more suitable than a hovering wrist.

scene gentlehome
when topic=home self.quarter=estate
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A meal on the Estate may travel several quiet turns before it reaches its place. | Some Estate corridors are at their most elegant when they allow a laden wolf space to pass.
b : How do you find your way? | Elegant floors or elegant manners?
a : By the last patch of light on each turn. And by remembering the guest ought to receive hot food. | Both give me pleasure. The manners are the part I actually need when my paws are occupied.

scene sharedsky
when topic=family self.married=yes self.spouse
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd save a turn at the high pane for #self.spouse# whenever the sky clears. | I'd put a warm plate aside for #self.spouse# while I waited for the first star.
b : Is there room for two? | Which do you serve first?
a : If we stand close. A perfectly reasonable arrangement for a married pair. | Supper if it's ready. A bright star will usually stay a little longer than a hot piece of fish.

scene quietfriend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd show #self.friend# a spoon with one star in the bowl and no better entertainment planned.
b : That little would do? | Could you put a second star there?
a : For a friend, quite. An ordinary pleasant thing doesn't always need a story round it. | If the angle were right. Sometimes the pleasure is in looking together and failing very gently.

scene campstar
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There was a hillside where the sky seemed nearly inside the door after dark. | A few flecks of charcoal can put a quiet high country evening back in my thoughts.
b : How near were the stars? | Did the little black pieces do that?
a : No nearer at all. The dark round them went on much further than any wall I knew. | The colour did. A black slope and one tiny point above it. A whole quiet night in a small impression.

scene clearpraise
when topic=gossip
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : Sometimes an ordinary helpful act gets retold as if it had been a great public performance. | I prefer leaving an unspoken kindness in the room where it was given.
b : Can praise be welcome? | Whose choice is it?
a : Not a sincere word. I mind an audience being invited where one wasn't sought. | I'd let the wolf who received it choose. The rest can go on with a sound clean silence.

scene quietfaith
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I give thanks for an evening star even on days the high pane has no view of it. | It's a comfort to me that a bright thing may be quite real beyond a patch of cloud.
b : Does the spoon have a part in prayer? | You don't need to see the star?
a : It reminds me to stop a moment. My prayer hardly depends upon polished cutlery. | I'd welcome the sight, certainly. I don't require the sky to make an arrangement for me every evening.

scene steelprice
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An old good spoon can be worth rather more than a new showy one with a thin bent handle.
b : How can you judge a spoon? | By the reflection?
a : How it rests empty across the fingers tells a good deal about what it will be like full. | For a pleasant experiment, yes. For supper I'd chiefly choose one that won't tip its contents into a fold.

scene shortsoft
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A modest supper may still arrive with its one best spoon turned neatly toward the guest. | There's no advantage to serving a small portion in a careless fashion.
b : Does that disguise the size? | Would you pretend it was a feast?
a : Not an attempt at disguise. I want the guest to know the care is still there. | No. I would let it be exactly as warm and pleasant as it truly can be.

scene starwish
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd enjoy a quiet seat high enough to see one star on the earliest clear evening of each season. | If I could add a little window anywhere it would be on a landing nobody hurries past laden.
b : For a star calendar? | Why a landing?
a : Merely to notice how things change. A new season shouldn't have to come with paperwork. | A glimpse can belong to every wolf on the stairs there. I'm rather fond of a view one can share.

grown

story wrongstar [topic=pastimes|memories]
  : I tried to show a bright little star on my spoon before supper and couldn't make it follow the curve properly. It remained squarely in the middle.
  : At last I realised it was a grain of salt from the preparation board.
  b : Did you wipe your star away?
  : Yes. I ought to have recognised a star that refused every known law of reflection.

story pairstep [topic=work|memories self.job=servant]
  : I came briskly up the last two risers with an empty tray and caught the setting sun low in its face. The whole landing took a little red glow.
  : I stopped so suddenly the cloth slid off my shoulder.
  b : Did anybody see the light?
  : I hope at least the wall enjoyed it. I finished by going back down one step for my cloth.

story snowdish [topic=weather|memories]
  : I put an empty dark dish outside once to see how quickly the first snow would cover the bottom. Tiny white stars came down all over it.
  : When I brought the dish inside it was full of a very little plain water.
  b : Was that a disappointment?
  : Not a bit. I knew what the small wet circle had looked like on the way in.

rule @pane
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One moment's light on the inside rim of the spoon. | Turn it a hair more. There is the star.

rule @service
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=servant
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A fresh spoon for the late place, please. | Set the handles towards the open edge facing the guest.

rule @snow
when concept=bark here.weather=snow
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Even the little scratched bowl borrows that snow light. | A pale sky caught on every clean surface.

rule @quiet
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The cloth can slide without a sound if the corners lie flat. | Keep one corner of the sill free for the view.

dlg resident.hub : You needn't wait for me to finish polishing. There's a quiet interval now.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, the little prospect in the spoon has been particularly fine of late.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : A very good hour for looking upward after the last bowl has been set down.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : A civil question carries quite adequately from your side of the table.
dlg resident.job [self.job=servant] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I remember the least conspicuous places as well as the grand chair at dinner.
dlg resident.job : I try to leave a place looking as if the wolf who next uses it were actually expected.
dlg resident.bye : I hope you look up once on your way home and find something worth the moment.

graft resident.hub
choice Can you show me the star on the spoon? -> turnspoon
node turnspoon
say Hold the bowl a little below your eye and let the bright side face the pane. Turn slowly. The star will come in at one edge when it happens to be visible.
free
choice And on a cloudy night? -> cloudspoon
choice I'll try the other angle. -> hub
node cloudspoon
say On a cloudy night we can have a clean spoon and a comfortable supper. There's no obligation on a small pleasure to perform every evening.
choice That sounds pleasant too. -> hub
choice Goodbye, and a clear sky. -> bye
